1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,445
Welcome to SmartClass AI.

2
00:00:01,445 --> 00:00:05,418
This walkthrough follows a class from the landing page through attendance

3
00:00:05,418 --> 00:00:06,140
and learning.

4
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:10,113
We will see teacher and student journeys, then explain how the

5
00:00:10,113 --> 00:00:12,280
system works using the project documentation.

6
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:15,793
The home page separates student and teacher spaces.

7
00:00:15,793 --> 00:00:18,428
Both enter one connected classroom platform.

8
00:00:18,428 --> 00:00:22,380
Teachers manage the class; students join and continue learning.

9
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:25,357
The Streamlit app coordinates screens and actions.

10
00:00:25,357 --> 00:00:29,186
Supabase stores profiles, attendance records, notes, and assessment data.

11
00:00:29,186 --> 00:00:33,865
Face and voice pipelines, Gemini, and email delivery support specific features.

12
00:00:33,865 --> 00:00:38,544
The architecture diagram traces a user action through the app and

13
00:00:38,544 --> 00:00:40,245
the services it calls.

14
00:00:40,245 --> 00:00:44,758
Student registration stores a name, a registration number, and a face

15
00:00:44,758 --> 00:00:45,168
profile.

16
00:00:45,168 --> 00:00:49,680
The face encoder turns an enrollment image into a numeric descriptor.

17
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:51,321
Voice enrollment is optional.

18
00:00:51,321 --> 00:00:55,834
During Face ID sign-in, a new capture is compared with stored

19
00:00:55,834 --> 00:00:58,295
profiles before the student workspace opens.

20
00:00:58,295 --> 00:01:02,669
After sign-in, the student sees enrolled subjects, assessments, and study tools.

21
00:01:02,669 --> 00:01:05,453
Quick Enrollment uses a teacher class code.

22
00:01:05,453 --> 00:01:09,827
The dashboard is the entry point to notes, attendance outlook, and

23
00:01:09,827 --> 00:01:11,020
peer study tools.

24
00:01:11,020 --> 00:01:15,577
The teacher workspace groups attendance, subject management, records, and course notes.

25
00:01:15,577 --> 00:01:20,134
A subject sets the class name and section; its join code

26
00:01:20,134 --> 00:01:20,962
connects students.

27
00:01:20,962 --> 00:01:25,105
Teachers can share notes and assessments from the same dashboard.

28
00:01:25,105 --> 00:01:29,286
For a large classroom, the teacher can add several photos from

29
00:01:29,286 --> 00:01:30,046
different angles.

30
00:01:30,046 --> 00:01:32,327
Overlapping views help cover the room.

31
00:01:32,327 --> 00:01:36,508
SmartClass processes each image and merges duplicate student matches across views.

32
00:01:36,508 --> 00:01:40,690
The class photos shown here are demo inputs, not an attendance

33
00:01:40,690 --> 00:01:41,830
decision by themselves.

34
00:01:41,830 --> 00:01:45,516
The attendance screen presents proposed present and absent results for the

35
00:01:45,516 --> 00:01:46,522
teacher to check.

36
00:01:46,522 --> 00:01:50,208
The sample recording shows four marked present and four absent from

37
00:01:50,208 --> 00:01:50,878
eight reviewed.

38
00:01:50,878 --> 00:01:54,564
A teacher checks the list before saving, so an AI suggestion

39
00:01:54,564 --> 00:01:56,910
does not silently become the class record.

40
00:01:56,910 --> 00:01:59,851
The documented face model produces a 128-value descriptor.

41
00:01:59,851 --> 00:02:03,895
The app compares it to enrolled students using Euclidean distance, where

42
00:02:03,895 --> 00:02:05,733
a smaller value is closer.

43
00:02:05,733 --> 00:02:09,409
The best match must be below zero point six zero.

44
00:02:09,409 --> 00:02:13,453
If the second-best match is within zero point zero five, it

45
00:02:13,453 --> 00:02:14,924
is treated as ambiguous.

46
00:02:14,924 --> 00:02:18,600
These thresholds are not a probability or a measured accuracy.

47
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:22,732
Teachers can attach PDFs, documents, slides, or images as course notes.

48
00:02:22,732 --> 00:02:26,864
The subject, title, and summary help students find the right material.

49
00:02:26,864 --> 00:02:30,996
Uploaded notes are stored for the class, then students can download

50
00:02:30,996 --> 00:02:33,250
or open them in the reader.

51
00:02:33,250 --> 00:02:37,334
The blackboard-to-notes tool accepts a board photo or a camera capture.

52
00:02:37,334 --> 00:02:41,047
Gemini reads the image and returns structured Markdown and LaTeX.

53
00:02:41,047 --> 00:02:45,131
The teacher can review and publish the resulting study guide to

54
00:02:45,131 --> 00:02:45,873
enrolled students.

55
00:02:45,873 --> 00:02:49,215
Generated content should be checked before it is shared.

56
00:02:49,215 --> 00:02:53,642
The Interactive Living Note Reader extracts readable content from common document

57
00:02:53,642 --> 00:02:54,044
formats.

58
00:02:54,044 --> 00:02:58,471
Students can listen to a note, ask a question, request a

59
00:02:58,471 --> 00:03:00,886
simpler explanation, or open an assessment.

60
00:03:00,886 --> 00:03:04,105
The selected note supplies context for that request.

61
00:03:04,105 --> 00:03:08,291
Teachers can create an assessment with instructions, a score limit, and

62
00:03:08,291 --> 00:03:10,574
an optional due date or attachment.

63
00:03:10,574 --> 00:03:13,238
Students see assigned assessments in their subject.

64
00:03:13,238 --> 00:03:17,423
Submission and grading follow the teacher settings; this screen shows the

65
00:03:17,423 --> 00:03:18,565
assignment setup flow.

66
00:03:18,565 --> 00:03:22,487
The documentation shows separate AI paths for board digitization, note explanations,

67
00:03:22,487 --> 00:03:23,557
and assistant questions.

68
00:03:23,557 --> 00:03:27,479
Each request sends selected text or an image with a task-specific

69
00:03:27,479 --> 00:03:31,045
prompt to Gemini, then returns the result to the app.

70
00:03:31,045 --> 00:03:34,967
There is no persistent vector search in this code, so AI

71
00:03:34,967 --> 00:03:37,820
answers should be checked against the source notes.

72
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:42,491
Students can open the Learning Hub for course notes, attendance-to-grade forecasts,

73
00:03:42,491 --> 00:03:45,039
study buddy matching, and voice profiles.

74
00:03:45,039 --> 00:03:49,285
The matcher uses enrolled classmates to build a collaborative challenge.

75
00:03:49,285 --> 00:03:53,956
It supports peer learning; generated questions are prompts to study together,

76
00:03:53,956 --> 00:03:55,230
not graded results.

77
00:03:55,230 --> 00:03:57,679
Voice attendance is a separate pipeline.

78
00:03:57,679 --> 00:04:02,169
A pretrained speaker encoder creates an embedding, and the app compares

79
00:04:02,169 --> 00:04:04,618
similarity against an enrolled voice profile.

80
00:04:04,618 --> 00:04:09,108
The documented cutoff is zero point six five, but the score

81
00:04:09,108 --> 00:04:10,332
is not confidence.

82
00:04:10,332 --> 00:04:14,822
The guide recommends consent, limited retention, and testing across representative classroom

83
00:04:14,822 --> 00:04:15,230
conditions.

84
00:04:15,230 --> 00:04:19,475
That is SmartClass AI: teacher tools for a class, and student

85
00:04:19,475 --> 00:04:21,404
tools to learn from it.

86
00:04:21,404 --> 00:04:25,649
See the included system documentation for full diagrams, formulas, and implementation

87
00:04:25,649 --> 00:04:26,035
notes.

88
00:04:24,700 --> 00:04:32,028
Start at the top: a teacher or student uses a browser,
which reaches the Streamlit interface over HTTPS.

89
00:04:32,248 --> 00:04:40,633
The Python server coordinates attendance, notes, and
assessments, then runs face and voice inference and
validates requests.

90
00:04:40,853 --> 00:04:49,401
It calls Supabase for records and files, Gemini for
study generation, and Abstract or Resend for email
services.

91
00:04:49,621 --> 00:04:56,196
Those services are separate from the app server, and
their secret credentials should stay server-side.

92
00:04:56,416 --> 00:05:00,666
This diagram follows one request from the browser to
the database.

93
00:05:00,886 --> 00:05:07,847
Streamlit receives the input, and server logic checks
it before running inference or calling an external
API.

94
00:05:08,068 --> 00:05:14,678
A result is presented for review where the feature
requires it; attendance suggestions must be checked by
the teacher.

95
00:05:14,898 --> 00:05:20,822
Only after the workflow completes does the app save
the resulting record to Supabase.

96
00:05:21,042 --> 00:05:26,682
The teacher first chooses a subject, which limits
matching to students enrolled in that class.

97
00:05:26,902 --> 00:05:34,832
The app accepts one to three photos, detects faces,
and converts each face into a one hundred twenty-eight
value descriptor.

98
00:05:35,052 --> 00:05:41,557
It compares each descriptor only with the class
roster, then merges repeated student IDs across
photos.

99
00:05:41,777 --> 00:05:49,622
The teacher reviews the proposed list and confirms it
before attendance logs are written; the app does not
stitch the photos together.

100
00:05:49,842 --> 00:05:58,037
For each detected face, the system measures Euclidean
distance from its descriptor to every enrolled
profile; smaller means closer.

101
00:05:58,257 --> 00:06:03,957
It sorts the candidates and accepts the best only when
the distance is at most zero point six zero.

102
00:06:04,177 --> 00:06:11,787
If there is a runner-up, the best must beat it by more
than zero point zero five; otherwise the result is
ambiguous and rejected.

103
00:06:12,007 --> 00:06:19,406
These are implementation thresholds, not a
probability, confidence score, or measured accuracy
claim.

104
00:06:19,626 --> 00:06:29,931
The left side is enrollment: a student records a voice
phrase, the app converts it to mono sixteen kilohertz
audio, trims silence, and stores a speaker embedding.

105
00:06:30,151 --> 00:06:37,506
For attendance, a class recording is split into speech
segments; very short segments under half a second are
skipped.

106
00:06:37,726 --> 00:06:43,436
The app embeds each remaining segment and compares it
with enrolled profiles using a dot product.

107
00:06:43,656 --> 00:06:51,323
Its best score for a student is accepted at zero point
six five or higher, then a teacher reviews and saves
the attendance.

108
00:06:51,543 --> 00:06:58,390
That score is not calibrated confidence; voice
enrollment and retention need clear consent and
safeguards.

109
00:06:58,610 --> 00:07:04,751
This diagram groups the learning features that send
task-specific prompts to Google Gemini.

110
00:07:04,971 --> 00:07:13,431
The assistant prepares a question, the board digitizer
adds a board image, and the interactive reader
extracts note text for question and answer.

111
00:07:13,651 --> 00:07:21,036
The simpler explanation tool has a text limit, while
study buddy uses subject information to prepare a peer
challenge.

112
00:07:21,256 --> 00:07:27,721
The dotted quiz helper is shown in the source diagram,
but the reviewed code has no user-interface caller for
it.

113
00:07:27,941 --> 00:07:35,274
Gemini returns generated text or a preview to the app;
check AI output against the original notes before
sharing it.

114
00:07:35,494 --> 00:07:42,499
The teacher flow starts with email and password
registration, followed by an advisory email reputation
check.

115
00:07:42,719 --> 00:07:49,183
The password is hashed with bcrypt before the teacher
record is stored in Supabase.

116
00:07:49,403 --> 00:07:57,608
After registration, the teacher creates a subject and
shares its join code, then manages attendance, notes,
and assessments.

117
00:07:57,828 --> 00:08:03,108
An email reputation check does not prove that the
teacher owns or can access the inbox.

118
00:08:03,328 --> 00:08:09,068
A student captures a face image, and registration
expects exactly one face in the frame.

119
00:08:09,288 --> 00:08:16,593
The app compares that face with existing profiles; it
either recognizes the student or continues profile
registration.

120
00:08:16,813 --> 00:08:22,858
The student then joins a subject with its class code
or QR link and can use study and attendance tools.

121
00:08:23,078 --> 00:08:30,741
Face matching can fail or be ambiguous, so provide a
normal recovery path and obtain consent for biometric
use.

122
00:08:30,961 --> 00:08:36,331
This diagram shows how the database links people,
classes, and learning records.

123
00:08:36,551 --> 00:08:44,496
A teacher owns subjects; students join subjects
through the subject students link table, which
represents many-to-many enrollment.

124
00:08:44,716 --> 00:08:52,141
Attendance logs connect one student and one subject
with a time and present status; notes and assessments
belong to a subject.

125
00:08:52,361 --> 00:09:00,616
A submission connects a student with an assessment and
stores its result or feedback, while uploaded files
live in storage and are referenced by path.

126
00:09:00,836 --> 00:09:08,931
The student record also contains face and voice
embeddings, so access, consent, and deletion controls
matter.

127
00:09:09,151 --> 00:09:13,881
The reset starts by looking up a teacher using the
submitted email address.

128
00:09:14,101 --> 00:09:22,096
The app generates a six-digit code, stores a keyed
digest with expiry and attempt limits, and asks Resend
to deliver the message.

129
00:09:22,316 --> 00:09:29,471
The teacher enters the code and a new password; after
verification, the app stores a new bcrypt hash.

130
00:09:29,691 --> 00:09:36,731
The email service sends the code, but the application
verifies it; the raw code is not kept as the durable
value.

131
00:09:36,951 --> 00:09:42,331
The browser is outside the trusted boundary, so every
input must be checked by the server.

132
00:09:42,551 --> 00:09:52,829
The Streamlit app should enforce ownership and
enrollment checks, and keep service-role, Gemini,
Resend, Abstract, and reset secrets on the server.

133
00:09:53,049 --> 00:09:59,963
Supabase, Gemini, and the email providers are external
services reached through server calls.

134
00:10:00,183 --> 00:10:08,238
The diagram explicitly says row-level security still
needs review; it is not evidence that every deployment
policy is already safe.

135
00:10:08,458 --> 00:10:14,878
Because face and voice biometrics are stored, limit
access and retention and explain the use to students.
